Dependency license supplements
=============================

Some published Rust crates omit their workspace's license files. manifest.json
maps exact package versions and license declarations to upstream license texts
from pinned source revisions. Each text has a source URL and SHA-256 digest;
identical texts are shared to avoid duplicating them in the source repository.
The package's declared authors are retained for attribution.

Where upstream provides only a license identifier or a link to its terms,
the corresponding standard MIT or CC0 text is also included. These standard
texts do not assert a new copyright holder or replace upstream notices.
The MIT option is used for packages offering MIT alongside other licenses.
Existing upstream statements about other available options remain intact.

The release builder combines these supplements with notices already present
in dependency archives, retaining nested license files and AUTHORS records.
It does not fetch license texts from the network. A dependency version or
license change requires reviewing the corresponding supplement again.
